{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RxNP2YcTpFpRpcitSVJteN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — distill_sparse_swiglu\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 2026 cycle)\n5\t- Deadline: 2026-05-25 (ARR submission)\n6\t- Track: Efficient Methods for NLP\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims\n9\t\n10\t1. **KL distillation discovers fundamentally different (and superior) neuron importance patterns that magnitude-based oracles miss**: The C1 causal ablation (D059) proves that KL's advantage comes **entirely** from target quality (which neurons to keep), with gradient coupling contributing ≈0 across **both PPL and all downstream tasks**. **Controlled eval (TEAL 50% uniform, matched protocol)**: BCE+KL-targets PPL = **11.9638**, KL predictor PPL = **11.9638** (exact match). **Downstream confirmation (full-spectrum)**: All 4 downstream tasks (ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K) also match within <1pp delta, confirming gradient coupling = 0 across PPL + reasoning + knowledge + math dimensions. Standard BCE (magnitude masks) PPL ≈ 22.51. Target quality alone accounts for KL's full advantage. *Additional evidence from training eval (Gumbel hard mask)*: BCE+KL-targets PPL 9.29 @60.9% ≈ KL 9.21 @60.6%, consistent with controlled eval. The 53% mask divergence between KL-derived and magnitude-based masks is the core empirical finding: KL discovers a qualitatively different neuron importance landscape. **Implication**: The gradient coupling analysis (§3.6) provides mathematical intuition for *why* KL can discover better targets (coupled gradients explore joint neuron interaction patterns), but the causal driver is the resulting mask quality, not the gradient pathway per se. This shifts the contribution from \"engineering a better loss\" to \"discovering that output-distribution distillation reveals hidden neuron importance structure.\" **Supporting evidence**: (a) Iso-compute ablation: BCE with 2.71× more FLOPs still PPL=27.97 vs KL=12.00, confirming the gap is structural; (b) BCE at recommended 30% operating point (D062): forced TEAL top-k PPL=11.24 vs KL=8.82, Δ=2.42 — BCE 30% is nearly as bad as KL 50% (11.80), meaning BCE's inferior masks waste ~20pp of sparsity budget; (c) BCE Lagrangian failure at 30%: BCE loss scale (~0.6) vs KL (~0.0001) causes same Lagrangian to fail; (d) No compensation needed: KL eliminates 67.2M compensation parameters (~256MB). **Anticipated attack**: \"Two-stage training (KL→oracle→BCE) avoids needing KL predictor at inference?\" Defense: KL predictor is contextual (per-input adaptive); oracle masks are fixed. Deployment requires per-input sparsity adaptation. **Remaining caveat**: Single seed (s42); C1 s123 in progress for statistical robustness. (Headline claim, resolves persistent R3-R8 confound)\n11\t\n12\t2. **SPON's static correction is orthogonal to KL and too weak to complement it**: Logit-space decomposition (plan_005) shows SPON's bias correction is near-orthogonal to KL's mask effect (cos_sim=0.196, per-layer ≤0) with only 15.8% relative magnitude. Cross-layer interaction is non-trivial (30.6%) but PPL recovery remains modest (7.3%, 0.23 PPL). Rather than KL \"subsuming\" SPON, the two target different error components—but SPON's component is too small to provide meaningful complementary benefit. Strengthens Claim 1: static correction is not just redundant but irrelevant to the dominant error mode that KL addresses. (Evidence: plan_005_subsumption_s42, spon_2048_s42, D009, D010)\n13\t\n14\t3. **Sparsity regime determines whether allocation or capacity is the bottleneck (phase transition finding)**: Empirical discovery from D030 uniform allocation experiments reveals a qualitative phase transition, not the originally predicted quadratic scaling. At ≤30% sparsity, global top-k causes high seed-to-seed variance in downstream metrics due to per-layer allocation imbalance (uniform allocation stabilizes MMLU: σ drops from 9.5pp to 1.3pp across 3 seeds, mean 40.7% vs TEAL's 38.6%). At ≥50%, model capacity itself is insufficient — no allocation strategy can recover (uniform MMLU=27.8%≈random). The transition reveals three distinct regimes with non-monotonic allocation preference: (1) **Budget-surplus regime (≤30%)**: uniform allocation reduces seed-to-seed instability by 7.5× (σ: 1.3pp vs 9.5pp across 3 seeds), stabilizing downstream performance (3-seed mean MMLU: 40.7±1.3pp uniform vs 35.7±9.5pp global); (2) **Budget-constrained regime (~40%)**: learned allocation outperforms blind uniformity — MMLU 38.1% (global) vs 30.7% (uniform), +7.4pp — the predictor's learned priorities become valuable when budget is tight; (3) **Capacity-cliff regime (≥50%)**: allocation irrelevant, both collapse to ~28% ≈ random. Recommended operating point (8B-validated): 30% sparsity with uniform allocation. At 30%, KL uniform dominates on the efficiency-quality Pareto frontier: PPL 8.82 vs TEAL 10.97 (−19.6%), with comparable-to-better downstream (MMLU +2.0pp, WG +2.5pp; ARC-c −1.5pp, GSM8K −0.5pp within noise). The advantage is primarily in PPL and knowledge-intensive tasks, not uniform across all benchmarks. **14B scale-dependent caveat (D054)**: At Qwen-2.5-14B 50% sparsity, uniform allocation does NOT fix KL's MMLU gap (64.49% uniform vs 63.72% global, only +0.77pp; TEAL global=71.83%). The 8B allocation-dependent pattern does not generalize to 14B. This is a valuable negative finding revealing loss × allocation × scale three-way interaction. 14B claim scope: KL PPL advantage preserved (7.62 vs 8.73 TEAL), but downstream MMLU gap persists regardless of allocation. The non-monotonic allocation preference (uniform@30% → global@40% → irrelevant@50%) provides mechanistic insight: at generous budgets, ensuring no layer is starved matters most; at tight budgets, the predictor's learned cross-layer priorities add value; at catastrophic budgets, capacity itself is the binding constraint. The failure mode changes qualitatively: allocation-fixable (≤30%) vs capacity-limited (≥50%). PPL non-monotonicity (40%=8.36 < 30%=8.82) while downstream is strictly monotonic further supports \"PPL is a poor proxy for downstream quality\" narrative. **6-point PPL regime curve (D063)**: 30%=8.82, 35%=9.31, 40%=10.12, 45%=10.80, 50%=11.80 (TEAL global). Smooth monotonic increase from 30-50%, providing dense sampling for regime boundary identification. 25% eval pending. This yields a practical deployment guideline and a mechanistic understanding of when/why sparse inference degrades. (Evidence: d030_kl30_uniform, d030_kl50_uniform, d030_kl40_uniform, bench_teal30, bench_teal50, bench_kl30_global, bench_kl50_global, lm_eval downstream series)\n15\t\n16\t## Story Spine\n17\t\n18\t- **Problem**: SwiGLU activation sparsity enables 40-60% neuron pruning at inference, but training-free heuristics (WINA/TEAL) leave a 6+ point quality gap, while learned BCE predictors require auxiliary compensation networks adding ~256MB overhead (FastForward).\n19\t\n20\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: (a) Training-free (WINA, TEAL, R-Sparse): no training cost, but quality gap too large for deployment. (b) Static learned (SPON): zero-overhead bias correction via KL distillation, but input-independent — cannot adapt to per-input neuron importance. (c) Contextual learned (FastForward): BCE predictor + compensation MLP, near-dense quality but inference overhead from compensation network. Gap: no prior work trains the contextual predictor itself with KL, and no work quantifies how much static correction remains useful once a coupled-loss contextual predictor is in place.\n21\t\n22\t- **Our framing / headline question**: \"What does KL distillation actually learn for SwiGLU sparsity prediction, and why do its masks differ fundamentally from magnitude-based oracles?\" The theoretical grounding (§3.6, suggestive): BCE gradient dL_BCE/ds_j depends only on neuron j (factorized), while KL gradient dL_KL/ds_j couples all active neurons through d_logits/dh * dh/dm. This provides intuition for how KL *can* discover joint interaction patterns. The C1 causal ablation (§4.4) then empirically confirms: the masks KL discovers, not the gradient pathway itself, are what matter.\n23\t\n24\t- **Headline result template**: \"KL-trained sparsity predictors discover neuron importance patterns that diverge 53% from magnitude-based masks. A causal ablation confirms that these mask patterns, not gradient coupling, drive KL's quality advantage: BCE trained on KL-derived masks matches KL performance exactly across PPL (11.96 = 11.96) and all downstream tasks (delta <1pp on ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K). This finding eliminates the need for 67.2M compensation parameters and reveals three sparsity operating regimes (now with 6 data points) with qualitatively different allocation requirements.\"\n25\t\n26\t## Two-Dimensional Taxonomy (Conceptual Contribution)\n27\t\n28\t|                          | Decomposed (BCE) | Intermediate (MSE) | Coupled (KL) |\n29\t|--------------------------|:-----------------:|:-------------------:|:-------------:|\n30\t| Static                   | —                 | —                   | SPON          |\n31\t| Per-layer                | —                 | ShadowLLM           | —             |\n32\t| Per-token contextual     | FastForward       | —                   | **Ours**      |\n33\t\n34\tPositions prior work and ours on two axes: correction granularity (static -> per-token) x training signal coupling (decomposed/BCE -> coupled/KL). Highlights the empty cell we fill.\n35\t\n36\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n37\t\n38\t1. **\"Incremental / no new algorithm\"**: **Substantially mitigated by C1 finding**. The 53% mask divergence and causal ablation are genuine empirical discoveries, not engineering contributions. No prior work has shown that KL-derived masks encode fundamentally different neuron importance from magnitude-based approaches. The paper now contributes a finding (mask pattern discovery) rather than just a method (combining known techniques). Additional support: formal decomposition framework, quantitative s^2 prediction, three-regime analysis.\n39\t\n40\t2. **\"KL wins only because more compute\"**: **Fully addressed** by iso-compute ablation (eval_bce_v3_s42): BCE with 2.71× more FLOPs → TEAL PPL=27.97 vs KL=12.00 (2.33× gap). BCE loss saturates, confirming structural mismatch not compute deficit.\n41\t\n42\t3. **\"Gumbel-sigmoid relaxation, not KL, explains gains\"**: Addressed by STE baseline (plan_002) isolating loss function contribution.\n43\t\n44\t4. **\"Single model / limited generalization\"**: Addressed by Mistral-7B-v0.3 (plan_009, GQA + sliding window) and Qwen-2.5-14B cross-scale validation (D048/D054). **14B mixed result**: KL PPL advantage preserved (7.62 vs TEAL 8.73, 1.47× dense ratio identical to 8B), but KL MMLU=63.72% (global) / 64.49% (uniform) significantly trails TEAL 71.83% (global). Uniform allocation does not fix this gap (D054). PPL-downstream disconnect at 14B scale is an honest limitation, not hidden. Framing: KL's coupled gradient captures output-distribution fidelity (PPL) across scales, but 14B knowledge-intensive tasks (MMLU) show scale-dependent sensitivity that warrants further investigation.\n45\t\n46\t5. **\"Effect size may not hold on downstream tasks\"**: Core defense: PPL + 4 discriminative tasks (ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K) under unified few-shot protocol across all conditions. LongBench (P1, if GPU budget allows) strengthens long-context coverage. MT-Bench deferred unless time permits — requires external LLM API for judging.\n47\t\n48\t6. **\"Unfair comparison: BCE+comp close to KL but at higher inference cost\"**: All result tables and figures must co-report quality AND inference cost (compensation params, per-token FLOPs, end-to-end latency). Efficiency-accuracy Pareto frontier (plan_007) is the definitive visualization. Even if BCE+comp matches KL on PPL, KL wins on the Pareto frontier — that IS the claim.\n49\t\n50\t## Venue Fit\n51\t- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: strong fit for activation sparsity + distillation\n52\t- NLP-specific evaluation (LongBench long-context, MT-Bench multi-turn) strengthens EMNLP fit vs pure systems venue\n53\t- **Novelty upgraded from R8**: C1 causal ablation + 53% mask divergence finding elevates paper from \"systematic composition\" to \"empirical discovery about what KL learns for sparsity prediction.\" This addresses the persistent R3-R8 novelty concern and moves the paper toward Main Conference territory (target 4.0).\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6c37791-8bb0-41a4-8393-79e1bd149b1f","uuid":"32c8125c-c905-485b-ace8-b4a741099432","timestamp":"2026-05-18T18:11:00.443Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_14/projects/distill_sparse_swiglu/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T173518/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — distill_sparse_swiglu\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 2026 cycle)\n- Deadline: 2026-05-25 (ARR submission)\n- Track: Efficient Methods for NLP\n\n## Core Claims\n\n1. **KL distillation discovers fundamentally different (and superior) neuron importance patterns that magnitude-based oracles miss**: The C1 causal ablation (D059) proves that KL's advantage comes **entirely** from target quality (which neurons to keep), with gradient coupling contributing ≈0 across **both PPL and all downstream tasks**. **Controlled eval (TEAL 50% uniform, matched protocol)**: BCE+KL-targets PPL = **11.9638**, KL predictor PPL = **11.9638** (exact match). **Downstream confirmation (full-spectrum)**: All 4 downstream tasks (ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K) also match within <1pp delta, confirming gradient coupling = 0 across PPL + reasoning + knowledge + math dimensions. Standard BCE (magnitude masks) PPL ≈ 22.51. Target quality alone accounts for KL's full advantage. *Additional evidence from training eval (Gumbel hard mask)*: BCE+KL-targets PPL 9.29 @60.9% ≈ KL 9.21 @60.6%, consistent with controlled eval. The 53% mask divergence between KL-derived and magnitude-based masks is the core empirical finding: KL discovers a qualitatively different neuron importance landscape. **Implication**: The gradient coupling analysis (§3.6) provides mathematical intuition for *why* KL can discover better targets (coupled gradients explore joint neuron interaction patterns), but the causal driver is the resulting mask quality, not the gradient pathway per se. This shifts the contribution from \"engineering a better loss\" to \"discovering that output-distribution distillation reveals hidden neuron importance structure.\" **Supporting evidence**: (a) Iso-compute ablation: BCE with 2.71× more FLOPs still PPL=27.97 vs KL=12.00, confirming the gap is structural; (b) BCE at recommended 30% operating point (D062): forced TEAL top-k PPL=11.24 vs KL=8.82, Δ=2.42 — BCE 30% is nearly as bad as KL 50% (11.80), meaning BCE's inferior masks waste ~20pp of sparsity budget; (c) BCE Lagrangian failure at 30%: BCE loss scale (~0.6) vs KL (~0.0001) causes same Lagrangian to fail; (d) No compensation needed: KL eliminates 67.2M compensation parameters (~256MB). **Anticipated attack**: \"Two-stage training (KL→oracle→BCE) avoids needing KL predictor at inference?\" Defense: KL predictor is contextual (per-input adaptive); oracle masks are fixed. Deployment requires per-input sparsity adaptation. **Remaining caveat**: Single seed (s42); C1 s123 in progress for statistical robustness. (Headline claim, resolves persistent R3-R8 confound)\n\n2. **SPON's static correction is orthogonal to KL and too weak to complement it**: Logit-space decomposition (plan_005) shows SPON's bias correction is near-orthogonal to KL's mask effect (cos_sim=0.196, per-layer ≤0) with only 15.8% relative magnitude. Cross-layer interaction is non-trivial (30.6%) but PPL recovery remains modest (7.3%, 0.23 PPL). Rather than KL \"subsuming\" SPON, the two target different error components—but SPON's component is too small to provide meaningful complementary benefit. Strengthens Claim 1: static correction is not just redundant but irrelevant to the dominant error mode that KL addresses. (Evidence: plan_005_subsumption_s42, spon_2048_s42, D009, D010)\n\n3. **Sparsity regime determines whether allocation or capacity is the bottleneck (phase transition finding)**: Empirical discovery from D030 uniform allocation experiments reveals a qualitative phase transition, not the originally predicted quadratic scaling. At ≤30% sparsity, global top-k causes high seed-to-seed variance in downstream metrics due to per-layer allocation imbalance (uniform allocation stabilizes MMLU: σ drops from 9.5pp to 1.3pp across 3 seeds, mean 40.7% vs TEAL's 38.6%). At ≥50%, model capacity itself is insufficient — no allocation strategy can recover (uniform MMLU=27.8%≈random). The transition reveals three distinct regimes with non-monotonic allocation preference: (1) **Budget-surplus regime (≤30%)**: uniform allocation reduces seed-to-seed instability by 7.5× (σ: 1.3pp vs 9.5pp across 3 seeds), stabilizing downstream performance (3-seed mean MMLU: 40.7±1.3pp uniform vs 35.7±9.5pp global); (2) **Budget-constrained regime (~40%)**: learned allocation outperforms blind uniformity — MMLU 38.1% (global) vs 30.7% (uniform), +7.4pp — the predictor's learned priorities become valuable when budget is tight; (3) **Capacity-cliff regime (≥50%)**: allocation irrelevant, both collapse to ~28% ≈ random. Recommended operating point (8B-validated): 30% sparsity with uniform allocation. At 30%, KL uniform dominates on the efficiency-quality Pareto frontier: PPL 8.82 vs TEAL 10.97 (−19.6%), with comparable-to-better downstream (MMLU +2.0pp, WG +2.5pp; ARC-c −1.5pp, GSM8K −0.5pp within noise). The advantage is primarily in PPL and knowledge-intensive tasks, not uniform across all benchmarks. **14B scale-dependent caveat (D054)**: At Qwen-2.5-14B 50% sparsity, uniform allocation does NOT fix KL's MMLU gap (64.49% uniform vs 63.72% global, only +0.77pp; TEAL global=71.83%). The 8B allocation-dependent pattern does not generalize to 14B. This is a valuable negative finding revealing loss × allocation × scale three-way interaction. 14B claim scope: KL PPL advantage preserved (7.62 vs 8.73 TEAL), but downstream MMLU gap persists regardless of allocation. The non-monotonic allocation preference (uniform@30% → global@40% → irrelevant@50%) provides mechanistic insight: at generous budgets, ensuring no layer is starved matters most; at tight budgets, the predictor's learned cross-layer priorities add value; at catastrophic budgets, capacity itself is the binding constraint. The failure mode changes qualitatively: allocation-fixable (≤30%) vs capacity-limited (≥50%). PPL non-monotonicity (40%=8.36 < 30%=8.82) while downstream is strictly monotonic further supports \"PPL is a poor proxy for downstream quality\" narrative. **6-point PPL regime curve (D063)**: 30%=8.82, 35%=9.31, 40%=10.12, 45%=10.80, 50%=11.80 (TEAL global). Smooth monotonic increase from 30-50%, providing dense sampling for regime boundary identification. 25% eval pending. This yields a practical deployment guideline and a mechanistic understanding of when/why sparse inference degrades. (Evidence: d030_kl30_uniform, d030_kl50_uniform, d030_kl40_uniform, bench_teal30, bench_teal50, bench_kl30_global, bench_kl50_global, lm_eval downstream series)\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: SwiGLU activation sparsity enables 40-60% neuron pruning at inference, but training-free heuristics (WINA/TEAL) leave a 6+ point quality gap, while learned BCE predictors require auxiliary compensation networks adding ~256MB overhead (FastForward).\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: (a) Training-free (WINA, TEAL, R-Sparse): no training cost, but quality gap too large for deployment. (b) Static learned (SPON): zero-overhead bias correction via KL distillation, but input-independent — cannot adapt to per-input neuron importance. (c) Contextual learned (FastForward): BCE predictor + compensation MLP, near-dense quality but inference overhead from compensation network. Gap: no prior work trains the contextual predictor itself with KL, and no work quantifies how much static correction remains useful once a coupled-loss contextual predictor is in place.\n\n- **Our framing / headline question**: \"What does KL distillation actually learn for SwiGLU sparsity prediction, and why do its masks differ fundamentally from magnitude-based oracles?\" The theoretical grounding (§3.6, suggestive): BCE gradient dL_BCE/ds_j depends only on neuron j (factorized), while KL gradient dL_KL/ds_j couples all active neurons through d_logits/dh * dh/dm. This provides intuition for how KL *can* discover joint interaction patterns. The C1 causal ablation (§4.4) then empirically confirms: the masks KL discovers, not the gradient pathway itself, are what matter.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"KL-trained sparsity predictors discover neuron importance patterns that diverge 53% from magnitude-based masks. A causal ablation confirms that these mask patterns, not gradient coupling, drive KL's quality advantage: BCE trained on KL-derived masks matches KL performance exactly across PPL (11.96 = 11.96) and all downstream tasks (delta <1pp on ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K). This finding eliminates the need for 67.2M compensation parameters and reveals three sparsity operating regimes (now with 6 data points) with qualitatively different allocation requirements.\"\n\n## Two-Dimensional Taxonomy (Conceptual Contribution)\n\n|                          | Decomposed (BCE) | Intermediate (MSE) | Coupled (KL) |\n|--------------------------|:-----------------:|:-------------------:|:-------------:|\n| Static                   | —                 | —                   | SPON          |\n| Per-layer                | —                 | ShadowLLM           | —             |\n| Per-token contextual     | FastForward       | —                   | **Ours**      |\n\nPositions prior work and ours on two axes: correction granularity (static -> per-token) x training signal coupling (decomposed/BCE -> coupled/KL). Highlights the empty cell we fill.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. **\"Incremental / no new algorithm\"**: **Substantially mitigated by C1 finding**. The 53% mask divergence and causal ablation are genuine empirical discoveries, not engineering contributions. No prior work has shown that KL-derived masks encode fundamentally different neuron importance from magnitude-based approaches. The paper now contributes a finding (mask pattern discovery) rather than just a method (combining known techniques). Additional support: formal decomposition framework, quantitative s^2 prediction, three-regime analysis.\n\n2. **\"KL wins only because more compute\"**: **Fully addressed** by iso-compute ablation (eval_bce_v3_s42): BCE with 2.71× more FLOPs → TEAL PPL=27.97 vs KL=12.00 (2.33× gap). BCE loss saturates, confirming structural mismatch not compute deficit.\n\n3. **\"Gumbel-sigmoid relaxation, not KL, explains gains\"**: Addressed by STE baseline (plan_002) isolating loss function contribution.\n\n4. **\"Single model / limited generalization\"**: Addressed by Mistral-7B-v0.3 (plan_009, GQA + sliding window) and Qwen-2.5-14B cross-scale validation (D048/D054). **14B mixed result**: KL PPL advantage preserved (7.62 vs TEAL 8.73, 1.47× dense ratio identical to 8B), but KL MMLU=63.72% (global) / 64.49% (uniform) significantly trails TEAL 71.83% (global). Uniform allocation does not fix this gap (D054). PPL-downstream disconnect at 14B scale is an honest limitation, not hidden. Framing: KL's coupled gradient captures output-distribution fidelity (PPL) across scales, but 14B knowledge-intensive tasks (MMLU) show scale-dependent sensitivity that warrants further investigation.\n\n5. **\"Effect size may not hold on downstream tasks\"**: Core defense: PPL + 4 discriminative tasks (ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K) under unified few-shot protocol across all conditions. LongBench (P1, if GPU budget allows) strengthens long-context coverage. MT-Bench deferred unless time permits — requires external LLM API for judging.\n\n6. **\"Unfair comparison: BCE+comp close to KL but at higher inference cost\"**: All result tables and figures must co-report quality AND inference cost (compensation params, per-token FLOPs, end-to-end latency). Efficiency-accuracy Pareto frontier (plan_007) is the definitive visualization. Even if BCE+comp matches KL on PPL, KL wins on the Pareto frontier — that IS the claim.\n\n## Venue Fit\n- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: strong fit for activation sparsity + distillation\n- NLP-specific evaluation (LongBench long-context, MT-Bench multi-turn) strengthens EMNLP fit vs pure systems venue\n- **Novelty upgraded from R8**: C1 causal ablation + 53% mask divergence finding elevates paper from \"systematic composition\" to \"empirical discovery about what KL learns for sparsity prediction.\" This addresses the persistent R3-R8 novelty concern and moves the paper toward Main Conference territory (target 4.0).\n","numLines":54,"startLine":1,"totalLines":54}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DhW9un2ZUhi5QuCEyzGPaB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"C1 Causal Ablation — seed 123 复现\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"C1 causal ablation 跨 seed 复现。BCE predictor 使用 KL s123 的 oracle masks (hard threshold) 作为 target 训练 1000 steps，然后在 TEAL uniform 50% 下评估 PPL 和 4 项 downstream tasks。 对比 KL s123 uniform 结果 (bench_kl50_uniform_s123: PPL=11.83, ARC-c=0.3515, WG=0.6298, MMLU=0.2751, GSM8K=0.0235)。s42 已验证 exact match (PPL delta=0.0000, max downstream delta=0.79pp)。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"wikitext2_ppl_teal_uniform\": 11.86,\n7\t      \"kl_s123_uniform_ppl_reference\": 11.83,\n8\t      \"ppl_delta\": 0.03,\n9\t      \"arc_challenge_acc_norm\": 0.346,\n10\t      \"winogrande_acc\": 0.636,\n11\t      \"mmlu_acc\": 0.2738,\n12\t      \"gsm8k_exact_match\": 0.022,\n13\t      \"arc_delta_vs_kl_pp\": -0.55,\n14\t      \"wg_delta_vs_kl_pp\": 0.62,\n15\t      \"mmlu_delta_vs_kl_pp\": -0.13,\n16\t      \"gsm8k_delta_vs_kl_pp\": -0.15,\n17\t      \"max_downstream_delta_pp\": 0.62,\n18\t      \"oracle_agreement_with_kl\": 0.977,\n19\t      \"final_bce_loss\": 0.056,\n20\t      \"training_sparsity\": 0.608,\n21\t      \"cross_seed_ppl_deltas\": [\n22\t        0.0,\n23\t        0.03\n24\t      ],\n25\t      \"cross_seed_max_downstream_deltas\": [\n26\t        0.79,\n27\t        0.62\n28\t      ]\n29\t    },\n30\t    \"tables\": [\n31\t      \"Table 4 (C1 Causal Ablation): 2×{PPL, ARC-c, WG, MMLU, GSM8K} cross-seed 矩阵，每 seed 一行\"\n32\t    ],\n33\t    \"figures\": [],\n34\t    \"analysis\": \"两个 seed PPL delta 分别为 0.00 和 0.03，远低于 0.05 threshold。Max downstream delta 分别为 0.79pp 和 0.62pp，远低于 1.5pp threshold。gradient coupling contribution 在两个 seed 上均 = 0，确认 target quality 是 KL 优势的 sole driver。这是论文最核心的 evidence， 直接将贡献从 \\\"engineering a better loss\\\" 提升为 \\\"discovering that output-distribution distillation reveals hidden neuron importance structure\\\"。\\n\\n\\nbest 档下 C1 跨 seed 复现的物理基础：KL 在不同 seed 下收敛到高度相似的 neuron importance landscape。s42 和 s123 的 KL predictor 虽然 random initialization 不同，但经过 1000 steps KL distillation 后，其 hard mask 与 magnitude oracle 的 divergence 均在 53%±2% 范围内 (teal_kl_overlap_corrected: z=7260, p<1e-10)。BCE+KL-targets 本质上在拟合这个 seed-stable 的 mask pattern，因此跨 seed PPL delta 应与 s42 (0.0000) 在同一量级。 s123 KL uniform PPL (11.83) 比 s42 (11.96) 略低 0.13，这个 seed-to-seed variance 是 Lagrangian controller 收敛路径的自然变异。BCE+KL-targets s123 将追踪到 11.83±0.05 内。 Downstream delta <1pp 的原因：在 50% uniform sparsity 下 downstream 已接近 random baseline (MMLU~27.5%, GSM8K~2%)，两种方法的 mask 都保留了相同的 minimum-viable neuron set， 差异被 downstream metric 的 noise floor (~0.5-1pp) 掩盖。\\n\"\n35\t  },\n36\t  {\n37\t    \"name\": \"6-Point Sparsity Regime Curve\",\n38\t    \"description\": \"补全 25% 数据点（kl_sparsity25_s42 已训练完成，实际 sparsity=0.23），加入已有 30-50% 数据， 构建 6-point PPL regime curve。同时生成 TEAL global 和 TEAL uniform 两种 allocation 的 curve。 涵盖 PREPARING 实验: kl_sparsity25_s42_eval_teal, kl_sparsity25_s42_eval_teal_uniform, kl_sparsity35_s42_eval_teal, kl_sparsity35_s42_eval_teal_uniform, kl_sparsity45_s42_eval_teal, kl_sparsity45_s42_eval_teal_uniform, kl_sparsity40_s42_eval_teal_uniform.\\n\",\n39\t    \"results\": {\n40\t      \"ppl_25_global\": 8.48,\n41\t      \"ppl_30_global\": 8.98,\n42\t      \"ppl_35_global\": 9.31,\n43\t      \"ppl_40_global\": 10.12,\n44\t      \"ppl_45_global\": 10.8,\n45\t      \"ppl_50_global\": 11.8,\n46\t      \"ppl_25_uniform\": 8.32,\n47\t      \"ppl_30_uniform\": 8.82,\n48\t      \"ppl_35_uniform\": 9.18,\n49\t      \"ppl_40_uniform\": 9.85,\n50\t      \"ppl_45_uniform\": 10.48,\n51\t      \"ppl_50_uniform\": 11.96,\n52\t      \"delta_25_30\": 0.5,\n53\t      \"delta_30_35\": 0.33,\n54\t      \"delta_35_40\": 0.81,\n55\t      \"delta_40_45\": 0.68,\n56\t      \"delta_45_50\": 1.0,\n57\t      \"regime_curve_monotonicity_violations\": 0,\n58\t      \"mmlu_25_uniform\": 0.448,\n59\t      \"arc_challenge_25_uniform\": 0.432,\n60\t      \"winogrande_25_uniform\": 0.708,\n61\t      \"gsm8k_25_uniform\": 0.094,\n62\t      \"mmlu_35_uniform\": 0.395,\n63\t      \"arc_challenge_35_uniform\": 0.412,\n64\t      \"winogrande_35_uniform\": 0.672,\n65\t      \"gsm8k_35_uniform\": 0.062,\n66\t      \"mmlu_45_uniform\": 0.318,\n67\t      \"arc_challenge_45_uniform\": 0.365,\n68\t      \"winogrande_45_uniform\": 0.648,\n69\t      \"gsm8k_45_uniform\": 0.032,\n70\t      \"allocation_crossover_sparsity\": 0.35,\n71\t      \"regime_1_surplus_boundary\": 0.3,\n72\t      \"regime_2_constrained_range\": \"35%-45%\",\n73\t      \"regime_3_cliff_onset\": 0.5\n74\t    },\n75\t    \"tables\": [\n76\t      \"Table 5 (Regime Curve): 6 rows × {Sparsity, PPL_uniform, PPL_global, Δ(uni-glo), MMLU, ARC-c, WG, GSM8K}\"\n77\t    ],\n78\t    \"figures\": [],\n79\t    \"analysis\": \"Curve 证明三个 regime 的定性不同: regime 1 (≤30%) downstream MMLU=44.8→40.6%（可用）， regime 2 (35-45%) MMLU=39.5→31.8%（degraded but structured），regime 3 (≥50%) MMLU=27.8%≈random（collapsed）。Global-uniform crossover 在 ~35% 为论文提供 actionable deployment guideline: 30% uniform 是 8B recommended operating point。6 个数据点的密度 足以精确定位 regime boundary 和 inflection point，比传统的 3-point sweep (30/50/70) 提供更有说服力的 empirical evidence。\\n\\n\\nbest 档下 6-point curve 单调的物理基础: sparsity 增加 = 保留更少 neurons = model capacity monotonically 下降。PPL 对 sparsity 的响应分三段： (1) 25-30% (surplus): 每 5pp sparsity 仅增 ~0.5 PPL，因为 pruned neurons 多为 low-importance (natural sparsity floor ~5%, sparsity_floor_extended)，uniform allocation 防止 layer starvation (global 30% retention analysis 显示 L27-L31 starved to 28-50%)。 (2) 35-45% (constrained): PPL 加速增长 (delta 0.68-1.00/5pp)，因为开始 prune functionally important neurons，global allocation 此时 outperform uniform 因为 predictor 的 learned per-layer priorities 能更好分配 tight budget (d030_kl40_uniform MMLU=30.7% vs global 38.1%)。 (3) ≥50% (cliff): PPL 跳升 +1.0/5pp，downstream collapse 到 near-random，allocation 差异 消失 (d030_kl50_uniform vs global: MMLU delta 仅 1.86pp, 不显著)。 25% 预测 PPL ~8.3-8.5 基于训练 loss 的 monotonic trend: 25% loss=0.158 < 30% loss=0.165 (kl_sparsity30_s42_v3)，差值 0.007 对应约 0.5 PPL 改善。\\n\"\n80\t  },\n81\t  {\n82\t    \"name\": \"BCE 30% Forced TEAL Top-k\",\n83\t    \"description\": \"BCE predictor (bce_30pct_s42, 已训练) 在 30% sparsity 下通过 forced TEAL top-k 评估。 对应 PREPARING 实验 bce_30pct_s42_eval。对比 KL 30% uniform (PPL=8.82) 量化 mask quality gap 在推荐操作点的大小。同时对比 vanilla TEAL 30% (PPL=10.97)。\\n\",\n84\t    \"results\": {\n85\t      \"wikitext2_ppl\": 11.24,\n86\t      \"arc_challenge_acc_norm\": 0.382,\n87\t      \"winogrande_acc\": 0.634,\n88\t      \"mmlu_acc\": 0.338,\n89\t      \"gsm8k_exact_match\": 0.056,\n90\t      \"ppl_gap_vs_kl30_uniform\": 2.42,\n91\t      \"ppl_gap_vs_teal30\": -0.27,\n92\t      \"mmlu_gap_vs_kl30_pp\": -6.8,\n93\t      \"mmlu_gap_vs_teal30_pp\": -4.8,\n94\t      \"bce_30_ppl\": 11.24,\n95\t      \"kl_50_global_ppl\": 11.8,\n96\t      \"ppl_proximity\": 0.56\n97\t    },\n98\t    \"tables\": [\n99\t      \"Table 2 新行: 30% operating point 三方对比 (KL uniform / TEAL vanilla / BCE forced)\"\n100\t    ],\n101\t    \"figures\": [],\n102\t    \"analysis\": \"2.42 PPL gap 在推荐操作点直接支撑 Claim 1 headline。BCE@30% (11.24) ≈ KL@50% (11.80) 是最直观的 \\\"mask matters\\\" evidence: 使用 BCE magnitude masks，需要额外保留 20% neurons 才能达到 KL 50% 的质量。BCE@30% 甚至不如 vanilla TEAL@30% (10.97)，说明 BCE predictor 学到的 mask pattern 比 activation magnitude heuristic 更差——因为 BCE 在 Lagrangian 约束 下可能过度 prune 某些 layers (BCE Lagrangian failure: loss scale ~0.6 vs KL ~0.0001, bce_gumbel_lagrangian_isolation best PPL=38.02 at 50%)。 MMLU gap -6.8pp vs KL30 进一步说明 BCE mask 在 knowledge-intensive tasks 上的劣势。\\n\\n\\nBCE 30% forced top-k PPL (~11.2) 接近 KL 50% (~11.8) 的原因是 BCE 的 magnitude-based mask 即使只 prune 30% 也选错 neurons。具体机制: (1) BCE gradient dL/ds_j = (σ(s_j) - t_j) · σ'(s_j) 仅依赖 neuron j 自身 target，无法 捕捉 joint interaction (gradient_snr_constrained_v2: SNR ratio=103.2x, KL gradient 信息量 远超 BCE)。 (2) BCE predictor 的 F1 vs magnitude oracle = 0.6128 (kl_bce_f1_oracle)，但这个 high F1 恰恰说明 BCE 学到的 pattern 与 magnitude oracle 高度相似。KL 的 F1 仅 0.5397 but PPL 远优，说明 KL 发现了 magnitude 未捕捉的 importance structure。 (3) BCE 在 30% 时 pruned 的 30% neurons 中包含 KL 认为重要的 neurons (53% mask divergence, z=7260)。这些 \\\"KL-important but magnitude-unimportant\\\" neurons 的 mean gate prob=0.614 (teal_kl_overlap_analysis)，说明它们有 moderate activation 但对 output distribution 贡献不成比例地大。 PPL=11.24 > best tier threshold 10.5 ✓，gap vs KL30 = 2.42 > 1.5 ✓。 BCE@30% (11.24) ≈ KL@50% (11.80) 意味着 BCE 的 inferior masks 浪费 ~20pp sparsity budget。\\n\"\n103\t  },\n104\t  {\n105\t    \"name\": \"LongBench Long-Context Evaluation\",\n106\t    \"description\": \"LongBench English subset (4K-32K tokens), 评估条件: KL 30% uniform, TEAL 30%, KL 50% global, TEAL 50%, dense baseline。Per-task-type: single-doc QA (NarrativeQA), multi-doc QA (Qasper, HotpotQA), summarization (GovReport, MultiNews)。 之前 6 次尝试中 5 次 failed (pipeline stability 是主要风险), v6 成功但 multi_news dense=2.5 疑似 eval bug。best 档假设 pipeline 问题彻底修复。\\n\",\n107\t    \"results\": {\n108\t      \"dense_narrativeqa\": 17.8,\n109\t      \"dense_qasper\": 24.6,\n110\t      \"dense_govreport\": 30.2,\n111\t      \"dense_multinews\": 25.8,\n112\t      \"dense_avg\": 24.6,\n113\t      \"kl30_narrativeqa\": 13.5,\n114\t      \"kl30_qasper\": 18.9,\n115\t      \"kl30_govreport\": 25.8,\n116\t      \"kl30_multinews\": 21.2,\n117\t      \"kl30_avg\": 19.9,\n118\t      \"kl30_retention_pct\": 80.9,\n119\t      \"teal30_narrativeqa\": 10.2,\n120\t      \"teal30_qasper\": 14.8,\n121\t      \"teal30_govreport\": 23.1,\n122\t      \"teal30_multinews\": 17.5,\n123\t      \"teal30_avg\": 16.4,\n124\t      \"teal30_retention_pct\": 66.7,\n125\t      \"kl50_narrativeqa\": 7.8,\n126\t      \"kl50_qasper\": 11.2,\n127\t      \"kl50_govreport\": 18.4,\n128\t      \"kl50_multinews\": 13.5,\n129\t      \"kl50_avg\": 12.7,\n130\t      \"teal50_narrativeqa\": 4.5,\n131\t      \"teal50_qasper\": 6.8,\n132\t      \"teal50_govreport\": 14.2,\n133\t      \"teal50_multinews\": 9.8,\n134\t      \"teal50_avg\": 8.8,\n135\t      \"kl30_vs_teal30_avg_delta\": 3.5\n136\t    },\n137\t    \"tables\": [\n138\t      \"Table 6 (LongBench): 5 conditions × 4+ tasks, per-task F1/ROUGE-L\"\n139\t    ],\n140\t    \"figures\": [],\n141\t    \"analysis\": \"KL30 avg retention ~81% vs TEAL30 ~67% 在长上下文维度进一步验证 mask quality advantage。 KL predictor 2K→32K generalization 支持 \\\"structural neuron importance\\\" 假设。 50% 条件下两者均大幅退化 (KL50 retention ~52%, TEAL50 ~36%)，与 short-context regime analysis 一致——50% 已进入 capacity-cliff regime，allocation 无关。 作为 P1 evidence，strengthen EMNLP venue fit (NLP-specific long-context evaluation)， 但非 core claim 支撑。pipeline 稳定性是主要 execution risk。\\n\\n\\nLongBench 评估 predictor 从 2048-token 训练序列到 4K-32K 测试序列的 generalization。 best 档下 KL30 retention ~81% 的逻辑: (1) KL predictor 学到的 neuron importance 主要反映 SwiGLU 的 structural property (哪些 neurons 对 output distribution 贡献最大)，这个 pattern 在不同 sequence length 下基本稳定——因为 importance 由 FFN weight structure 决定，不由 sequence position 决定。 (2) 30% sparsity 处于 budget-surplus regime，natural sparsity floor (~5%) 的 neurons 在长序列下同样 inactive (sparsity_floor_extended: floor_30pct=0.0499)。 (3) Summarization (GovReport) retention 最高 (85%) 因为 summarization 主要依赖 dominant activation mode，对 minor neuron pruning 最 robust。QA tasks (NarrativeQA) retention 较低 (76%) 因为需要精确 retrieval + reasoning 链。 (4) TEAL 30% retention 更低 (67%) 因为 magnitude-based mask 在长上下文下的 layer allocation error 累积更严重——长序列的 attention pattern 变化导致不同 layer 的 importance re-ranking，static magnitude 无法 adapt。 注意: pipeline 之前连续 5 次 failed，best 档假设评估脚本 debug 完成 (修复 tokenization truncation、generation config、metric computation 等问题)。这是 best 档的一个强假设。\\n\"\n142\t  },\n143\t  {\n144\t    \"name\": \"MT-Bench Multi-Turn Evaluation\",\n145\t    \"description\": \"MT-Bench 80 multi-turn questions, 8 categories, GPT-4o judge。 条件: Dense, KL 30% uniform, TEAL 30%。P2 priority, 仅在 GPU budget 和时间允许时执行。 注意: 使用 Llama 3.1 8B base model (非 instruct)，base model 在 instruction-following 任务上表现有限，绝对分数会较低。主要价值在 relative comparison。\\n\",\n146\t    \"results\": {\n147\t      \"dense_avg_score\": 4.15,\n148\t      \"kl30_avg_score\": 3.82,\n149\t      \"teal30_avg_score\": 3.28,\n150\t      \"kl30_retention_pct\": 92.0,\n151\t      \"teal30_retention_pct\": 79.0,\n152\t      \"kl30_writing\": 4.25,\n153\t      \"kl30_roleplay\": 4.1,\n154\t      \"kl30_reasoning\": 3.45,\n155\t      \"kl30_math\": 2.85,\n156\t      \"kl30_coding\": 3.5,\n157\t      \"kl30_extraction\": 4.35,\n158\t      \"kl30_stem\": 3.8,\n159\t      \"kl30_humanities\": 4.25,\n160\t      \"kl30_math_delta_vs_dense\": -0.55,\n161\t      \"kl30_avg_delta_vs_dense\": -0.33\n162\t    },\n163\t    \"tables\": [\n164\t      \"Table 7 (MT-Bench): 3 conditions × 8 categories + average, 注明 base model\"\n165\t    ],\n166\t    \"figures\": [],\n167\t    \"analysis\": \"MT-Bench relative ordering confirms KL advantage extends to generative quality, not just discriminative benchmarks。但 base model 绝对分数低 (~4/10) 限制了 这个 evidence 的说服力。审稿人可能 discount base model MT-Bench。 如果 GPU budget 不足应优先 drop 此实验。核心 claims 不依赖此结果。\\n\\n\\nbase model (非 instruct-tuned) 在 MT-Bench 上绝对分数有限 (~4/10)，因为 base model 缺乏 instruction-following alignment。但 relative ordering 仍有诊断价值: (1) KL30 retention ~92% (3.82/4.15) 高于短序列 downstream 的 retention (~85-90% on most tasks)，因为 MT-Bench 的 multi-turn format 更依赖 language modeling fluency (KL 直接优化的 objective) 而非 precise factual recall。 (2) Math/reasoning categories 退化最大 (~0.5 points) 因为这些 task 需要 precise step-by-step computation，每步的 sparse mask error 会 compound。 (3) Writing/humanities 几乎不受影响因为这些 task 依赖 dominant language patterns (high-activation neurons, natural sparsity floor 内保留的 neurons)。 (4) TEAL30 在 math/reasoning 上更差因为 magnitude mask 无法 preserve output distribution 的 tail (长尾 token predictions)，而 math 答案通常在 vocabulary distribution 的 tail 中。 base model 限制使 MT-Bench 的绝对值意义有限，但 \\\"KL 在 multi-turn generation 下 near-dense quality\\\" 的 relative finding 仍有叙事价值。\\n\"\n168\t  },\n169\t  {\n170\t    \"name\": \"RULER Synthetic Long-Context Diagnostics\",\n171\t    \"description\": \"RULER synthetic evaluation at 4K and 16K context, 3 task types: NIAH (needle-in-a-haystack), multi-key retrieval, variable tracking。 Fine-grained diagnostic complementing LongBench。P2 priority, deps on plan_010。\\n\",\n172\t    \"results\": {\n173\t      \"dense_4k_niah\": 92.5,\n174\t      \"dense_4k_multikey\": 78.3,\n175\t      \"dense_4k_vartrack\": 75.8,\n176\t      \"dense_4k_avg\": 82.2,\n177\t      \"kl30_4k_niah\": 88.2,\n178\t      \"kl30_4k_multikey\": 71.5,\n179\t      \"kl30_4k_vartrack\": 68.4,\n180\t      \"kl30_4k_avg\": 76.0,\n181\t      \"teal30_4k_niah\": 80.5,\n182\t      \"teal30_4k_multikey\": 58.2,\n183\t      \"teal30_4k_vartrack\": 55.8,\n184\t      \"teal30_4k_avg\": 64.8,\n185\t      \"dense_16k_niah\": 85.1,\n186\t      \"dense_16k_multikey\": 62.4,\n187\t      \"dense_16k_vartrack\": 58.2,\n188\t      \"dense_16k_avg\": 68.6,\n189\t      \"kl30_16k_niah\": 78.5,\n190\t      \"kl30_16k_multikey\": 53.8,\n191\t      \"kl30_16k_vartrack\": 49.2,\n192\t      \"kl30_16k_avg\": 60.5,\n193\t      \"teal30_16k_niah\": 68.2,\n194\t      \"teal30_16k_multikey\": 40.5,\n195\t      \"teal30_16k_vartrack\": 38.6,\n196\t      \"teal30_16k_avg\": 49.1,\n197\t      \"kl30_4k_to_16k_drop\": 15.5,\n198\t      \"dense_4k_to_16k_drop\": 13.6,\n199\t      \"teal30_4k_to_16k_drop\": 15.7\n200\t    },\n201\t    \"tables\": [\n202\t      \"Table 8 (RULER): 3 conditions × 3 tasks × 2 lengths\"\n203\t    ],\n204\t    \"figures\": [],\n205\t    \"analysis\": \"RULER 提供 fine-grained diagnostic: KL 的 advantage 在 multi-key 和 variable tracking 上最显著 (13-15pp over TEAL at 4K)，在 NIAH 上最小 (~8pp)。这与 \\\"KL captures joint neuron interaction\\\" 叙事一致——需要 multi-pattern activation 的 task 受益最大。 16K 数据表明 sparsity-induced degradation 不随 context length 加速， strengthening generalization claim。作为 P2，non-essential for core claims。\\n\\nRULER synthetic tasks 不需要 instruction following (与 MT-Bench 不同)，因此 base model 可以提供有意义的绝对分数。 (1) NIAH 对 sparsity 最 robust (KL30 retention 95% at 4K) 因为 needle retrieval 主要依赖 attention 定位 (未被 sparse)，FFN 只需 extract 和 copy 信息。 (2) Multi-key retrieval 和 variable tracking 对 sparsity 更敏感 (retention ~85-90%) 因为需要 FFN 同时处理多个 scattered information，neuron interaction quality 直接影响 cross-position information aggregation。 (3) 4K→16K degradation pattern: KL30 的 degradation rate (15.5pp) 接近 dense (13.6pp)， 而 TEAL30 (15.7pp) 与 KL30 相近。这说明 degradation 主要来自 Llama 3.1 8B 的 intrinsic long-context 能力限制，而非 sparsity 引入的额外退化。 (4) KL 在 multi-key task 上的优势最大 (KL 71.5 vs TEAL 58.2 at 4K)，因为 multi-key 需要 FFN 同时 activate 多个 retrieval patterns，KL 的 joint-interaction-aware masks 比 magnitude masks 更好地保留了这种 multi-pattern capacity。\\n\"\n206\t  }\n207\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6c37791-8bb0-41a4-8393-79e1bd149b1f","uuid":"b0371ccc-9f51-4911-a8f4-af1b47e04de2","timestamp":"2026-05-18T18:11:00.580Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_14/projects/distill_sparse_swiglu/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T173518/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"C1 Causal Ablation — seed 123 复现\",\n    \"description\": \"C1 causal ablation 跨 seed 复现。BCE predictor 使用 KL s123 的 oracle masks (hard threshold) 作为 target 训练 1000 steps，然后在 TEAL uniform 50% 下评估 PPL 和 4 项 downstream tasks。 对比 KL s123 uniform 结果 (bench_kl50_uniform_s123: PPL=11.83, ARC-c=0.3515, WG=0.6298, MMLU=0.2751, GSM8K=0.0235)。s42 已验证 exact match (PPL delta=0.0000, max downstream delta=0.79pp)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"wikitext2_ppl_teal_uniform\": 11.86,\n      \"kl_s123_uniform_ppl_reference\": 11.83,\n      \"ppl_delta\": 0.03,\n      \"arc_challenge_acc_norm\": 0.346,\n      \"winogrande_acc\": 0.636,\n      \"mmlu_acc\": 0.2738,\n      \"gsm8k_exact_match\": 0.022,\n      \"arc_delta_vs_kl_pp\": -0.55,\n      \"wg_delta_vs_kl_pp\": 0.62,\n      \"mmlu_delta_vs_kl_pp\": -0.13,\n      \"gsm8k_delta_vs_kl_pp\": -0.15,\n      \"max_downstream_delta_pp\": 0.62,\n      \"oracle_agreement_with_kl\": 0.977,\n      \"final_bce_loss\": 0.056,\n      \"training_sparsity\": 0.608,\n      \"cross_seed_ppl_deltas\": [\n        0.0,\n        0.03\n      ],\n      \"cross_seed_max_downstream_deltas\": [\n        0.79,\n        0.62\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4 (C1 Causal Ablation): 2×{PPL, ARC-c, WG, MMLU, GSM8K} cross-seed 矩阵，每 seed 一行\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"两个 seed PPL delta 分别为 0.00 和 0.03，远低于 0.05 threshold。Max downstream delta 分别为 0.79pp 和 0.62pp，远低于 1.5pp threshold。gradient coupling contribution 在两个 seed 上均 = 0，确认 target quality 是 KL 优势的 sole driver。这是论文最核心的 evidence， 直接将贡献从 \\\"engineering a better loss\\\" 提升为 \\\"discovering that output-distribution distillation reveals hidden neuron importance structure\\\"。\\n\\n\\nbest 档下 C1 跨 seed 复现的物理基础：KL 在不同 seed 下收敛到高度相似的 neuron importance landscape。s42 和 s123 的 KL predictor 虽然 random initialization 不同，但经过 1000 steps KL distillation 后，其 hard mask 与 magnitude oracle 的 divergence 均在 53%±2% 范围内 (teal_kl_overlap_corrected: z=7260, p<1e-10)。BCE+KL-targets 本质上在拟合这个 seed-stable 的 mask pattern，因此跨 seed PPL delta 应与 s42 (0.0000) 在同一量级。 s123 KL uniform PPL (11.83) 比 s42 (11.96) 略低 0.13，这个 seed-to-seed variance 是 Lagrangian controller 收敛路径的自然变异。BCE+KL-targets s123 将追踪到 11.83±0.05 内。 Downstream delta <1pp 的原因：在 50% uniform sparsity 下 downstream 已接近 random baseline (MMLU~27.5%, GSM8K~2%)，两种方法的 mask 都保留了相同的 minimum-viable neuron set， 差异被 downstream metric 的 noise floor (~0.5-1pp) 掩盖。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"6-Point Sparsity Regime Curve\",\n    \"description\": \"补全 25% 数据点（kl_sparsity25_s42 已训练完成，实际 sparsity=0.23），加入已有 30-50% 数据， 构建 6-point PPL regime curve。同时生成 TEAL global 和 TEAL uniform 两种 allocation 的 curve。 涵盖 PREPARING 实验: kl_sparsity25_s42_eval_teal, kl_sparsity25_s42_eval_teal_uniform, kl_sparsity35_s42_eval_teal, kl_sparsity35_s42_eval_teal_uniform, kl_sparsity45_s42_eval_teal, kl_sparsity45_s42_eval_teal_uniform, kl_sparsity40_s42_eval_teal_uniform.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ppl_25_global\": 8.48,\n      \"ppl_30_global\": 8.98,\n      \"ppl_35_global\": 9.31,\n      \"ppl_40_global\": 10.12,\n      \"ppl_45_global\": 10.8,\n      \"ppl_50_global\": 11.8,\n      \"ppl_25_uniform\": 8.32,\n      \"ppl_30_uniform\": 8.82,\n      \"ppl_35_uniform\": 9.18,\n      \"ppl_40_uniform\": 9.85,\n      \"ppl_45_uniform\": 10.48,\n      \"ppl_50_uniform\": 11.96,\n      \"delta_25_30\": 0.5,\n      \"delta_30_35\": 0.33,\n      \"delta_35_40\": 0.81,\n      \"delta_40_45\": 0.68,\n      \"delta_45_50\": 1.0,\n      \"regime_curve_monotonicity_violations\": 0,\n      \"mmlu_25_uniform\": 0.448,\n      \"arc_challenge_25_uniform\": 0.432,\n      \"winogrande_25_uniform\": 0.708,\n      \"gsm8k_25_uniform\": 0.094,\n      \"mmlu_35_uniform\": 0.395,\n      \"arc_challenge_35_uniform\": 0.412,\n      \"winogrande_35_uniform\": 0.672,\n      \"gsm8k_35_uniform\": 0.062,\n      \"mmlu_45_uniform\": 0.318,\n      \"arc_challenge_45_uniform\": 0.365,\n      \"winogrande_45_uniform\": 0.648,\n      \"gsm8k_45_uniform\": 0.032,\n      \"allocation_crossover_sparsity\": 0.35,\n      \"regime_1_surplus_boundary\": 0.3,\n      \"regime_2_constrained_range\": \"35%-45%\",\n      \"regime_3_cliff_onset\": 0.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5 (Regime Curve): 6 rows × {Sparsity, PPL_uniform, PPL_global, Δ(uni-glo), MMLU, ARC-c, WG, GSM8K}\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Curve 证明三个 regime 的定性不同: regime 1 (≤30%) downstream MMLU=44.8→40.6%（可用）， regime 2 (35-45%) MMLU=39.5→31.8%（degraded but structured），regime 3 (≥50%) MMLU=27.8%≈random（collapsed）。Global-uniform crossover 在 ~35% 为论文提供 actionable deployment guideline: 30% uniform 是 8B recommended operating point。6 个数据点的密度 足以精确定位 regime boundary 和 inflection point，比传统的 3-point sweep (30/50/70) 提供更有说服力的 empirical evidence。\\n\\n\\nbest 档下 6-point curve 单调的物理基础: sparsity 增加 = 保留更少 neurons = model capacity monotonically 下降。PPL 对 sparsity 的响应分三段： (1) 25-30% (surplus): 每 5pp sparsity 仅增 ~0.5 PPL，因为 pruned neurons 多为 low-importance (natural sparsity floor ~5%, sparsity_floor_extended)，uniform allocation 防止 layer starvation (global 30% retention analysis 显示 L27-L31 starved to 28-50%)。 (2) 35-45% (constrained): PPL 加速增长 (delta 0.68-1.00/5pp)，因为开始 prune functionally important neurons，global allocation 此时 outperform uniform 因为 predictor 的 learned per-layer priorities 能更好分配 tight budget (d030_kl40_uniform MMLU=30.7% vs global 38.1%)。 (3) ≥50% (cliff): PPL 跳升 +1.0/5pp，downstream collapse 到 near-random，allocation 差异 消失 (d030_kl50_uniform vs global: MMLU delta 仅 1.86pp, 不显著)。 25% 预测 PPL ~8.3-8.5 基于训练 loss 的 monotonic trend: 25% loss=0.158 < 30% loss=0.165 (kl_sparsity30_s42_v3)，差值 0.007 对应约 0.5 PPL 改善。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"BCE 30% Forced TEAL Top-k\",\n    \"description\": \"BCE predictor (bce_30pct_s42, 已训练) 在 30% sparsity 下通过 forced TEAL top-k 评估。 对应 PREPARING 实验 bce_30pct_s42_eval。对比 KL 30% uniform (PPL=8.82) 量化 mask quality gap 在推荐操作点的大小。同时对比 vanilla TEAL 30% (PPL=10.97)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"wikitext2_ppl\": 11.24,\n      \"arc_challenge_acc_norm\": 0.382,\n      \"winogrande_acc\": 0.634,\n      \"mmlu_acc\": 0.338,\n      \"gsm8k_exact_match\": 0.056,\n      \"ppl_gap_vs_kl30_uniform\": 2.42,\n      \"ppl_gap_vs_teal30\": -0.27,\n      \"mmlu_gap_vs_kl30_pp\": -6.8,\n      \"mmlu_gap_vs_teal30_pp\": -4.8,\n      \"bce_30_ppl\": 11.24,\n      \"kl_50_global_ppl\": 11.8,\n      \"ppl_proximity\": 0.56\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2 新行: 30% operating point 三方对比 (KL uniform / TEAL vanilla / BCE forced)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"2.42 PPL gap 在推荐操作点直接支撑 Claim 1 headline。BCE@30% (11.24) ≈ KL@50% (11.80) 是最直观的 \\\"mask matters\\\" evidence: 使用 BCE magnitude masks，需要额外保留 20% neurons 才能达到 KL 50% 的质量。BCE@30% 甚至不如 vanilla TEAL@30% (10.97)，说明 BCE predictor 学到的 mask pattern 比 activation magnitude heuristic 更差——因为 BCE 在 Lagrangian 约束 下可能过度 prune 某些 layers (BCE Lagrangian failure: loss scale ~0.6 vs KL ~0.0001, bce_gumbel_lagrangian_isolation best PPL=38.02 at 50%)。 MMLU gap -6.8pp vs KL30 进一步说明 BCE mask 在 knowledge-intensive tasks 上的劣势。\\n\\n\\nBCE 30% forced top-k PPL (~11.2) 接近 KL 50% (~11.8) 的原因是 BCE 的 magnitude-based mask 即使只 prune 30% 也选错 neurons。具体机制: (1) BCE gradient dL/ds_j = (σ(s_j) - t_j) · σ'(s_j) 仅依赖 neuron j 自身 target，无法 捕捉 joint interaction (gradient_snr_constrained_v2: SNR ratio=103.2x, KL gradient 信息量 远超 BCE)。 (2) BCE predictor 的 F1 vs magnitude oracle = 0.6128 (kl_bce_f1_oracle)，但这个 high F1 恰恰说明 BCE 学到的 pattern 与 magnitude oracle 高度相似。KL 的 F1 仅 0.5397 but PPL 远优，说明 KL 发现了 magnitude 未捕捉的 importance structure。 (3) BCE 在 30% 时 pruned 的 30% neurons 中包含 KL 认为重要的 neurons (53% mask divergence, z=7260)。这些 \\\"KL-important but magnitude-unimportant\\\" neurons 的 mean gate prob=0.614 (teal_kl_overlap_analysis)，说明它们有 moderate activation 但对 output distribution 贡献不成比例地大。 PPL=11.24 > best tier threshold 10.5 ✓，gap vs KL30 = 2.42 > 1.5 ✓。 BCE@30% (11.24) ≈ KL@50% (11.80) 意味着 BCE 的 inferior masks 浪费 ~20pp sparsity budget。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"LongBench Long-Context Evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"LongBench English subset (4K-32K tokens), 评估条件: KL 30% uniform, TEAL 30%, KL 50% global, TEAL 50%, dense baseline。Per-task-type: single-doc QA (NarrativeQA), multi-doc QA (Qasper, HotpotQA), summarization (GovReport, MultiNews)。 之前 6 次尝试中 5 次 failed (pipeline stability 是主要风险), v6 成功但 multi_news dense=2.5 疑似 eval bug。best 档假设 pipeline 问题彻底修复。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_narrativeqa\": 17.8,\n      \"dense_qasper\": 24.6,\n      \"dense_govreport\": 30.2,\n      \"dense_multinews\": 25.8,\n      \"dense_avg\": 24.6,\n      \"kl30_narrativeqa\": 13.5,\n      \"kl30_qasper\": 18.9,\n      \"kl30_govreport\": 25.8,\n      \"kl30_multinews\": 21.2,\n      \"kl30_avg\": 19.9,\n      \"kl30_retention_pct\": 80.9,\n      \"teal30_narrativeqa\": 10.2,\n      \"teal30_qasper\": 14.8,\n      \"teal30_govreport\": 23.1,\n      \"teal30_multinews\": 17.5,\n      \"teal30_avg\": 16.4,\n      \"teal30_retention_pct\": 66.7,\n      \"kl50_narrativeqa\": 7.8,\n      \"kl50_qasper\": 11.2,\n      \"kl50_govreport\": 18.4,\n      \"kl50_multinews\": 13.5,\n      \"kl50_avg\": 12.7,\n      \"teal50_narrativeqa\": 4.5,\n      \"teal50_qasper\": 6.8,\n      \"teal50_govreport\": 14.2,\n      \"teal50_multinews\": 9.8,\n      \"teal50_avg\": 8.8,\n      \"kl30_vs_teal30_avg_delta\": 3.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6 (LongBench): 5 conditions × 4+ tasks, per-task F1/ROUGE-L\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"KL30 avg retention ~81% vs TEAL30 ~67% 在长上下文维度进一步验证 mask quality advantage。 KL predictor 2K→32K generalization 支持 \\\"structural neuron importance\\\" 假设。 50% 条件下两者均大幅退化 (KL50 retention ~52%, TEAL50 ~36%)，与 short-context regime analysis 一致——50% 已进入 capacity-cliff regime，allocation 无关。 作为 P1 evidence，strengthen EMNLP venue fit (NLP-specific long-context evaluation)， 但非 core claim 支撑。pipeline 稳定性是主要 execution risk。\\n\\n\\nLongBench 评估 predictor 从 2048-token 训练序列到 4K-32K 测试序列的 generalization。 best 档下 KL30 retention ~81% 的逻辑: (1) KL predictor 学到的 neuron importance 主要反映 SwiGLU 的 structural property (哪些 neurons 对 output distribution 贡献最大)，这个 pattern 在不同 sequence length 下基本稳定——因为 importance 由 FFN weight structure 决定，不由 sequence position 决定。 (2) 30% sparsity 处于 budget-surplus regime，natural sparsity floor (~5%) 的 neurons 在长序列下同样 inactive (sparsity_floor_extended: floor_30pct=0.0499)。 (3) Summarization (GovReport) retention 最高 (85%) 因为 summarization 主要依赖 dominant activation mode，对 minor neuron pruning 最 robust。QA tasks (NarrativeQA) retention 较低 (76%) 因为需要精确 retrieval + reasoning 链。 (4) TEAL 30% retention 更低 (67%) 因为 magnitude-based mask 在长上下文下的 layer allocation error 累积更严重——长序列的 attention pattern 变化导致不同 layer 的 importance re-ranking，static magnitude 无法 adapt。 注意: pipeline 之前连续 5 次 failed，best 档假设评估脚本 debug 完成 (修复 tokenization truncation、generation config、metric computation 等问题)。这是 best 档的一个强假设。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"MT-Bench Multi-Turn Evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"MT-Bench 80 multi-turn questions, 8 categories, GPT-4o judge。 条件: Dense, KL 30% uniform, TEAL 30%。P2 priority, 仅在 GPU budget 和时间允许时执行。 注意: 使用 Llama 3.1 8B base model (非 instruct)，base model 在 instruction-following 任务上表现有限，绝对分数会较低。主要价值在 relative comparison。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_avg_score\": 4.15,\n      \"kl30_avg_score\": 3.82,\n      \"teal30_avg_score\": 3.28,\n      \"kl30_retention_pct\": 92.0,\n      \"teal30_retention_pct\": 79.0,\n      \"kl30_writing\": 4.25,\n      \"kl30_roleplay\": 4.1,\n      \"kl30_reasoning\": 3.45,\n      \"kl30_math\": 2.85,\n      \"kl30_coding\": 3.5,\n      \"kl30_extraction\": 4.35,\n      \"kl30_stem\": 3.8,\n      \"kl30_humanities\": 4.25,\n      \"kl30_math_delta_vs_dense\": -0.55,\n      \"kl30_avg_delta_vs_dense\": -0.33\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7 (MT-Bench): 3 conditions × 8 categories + average, 注明 base model\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"MT-Bench relative ordering confirms KL advantage extends to generative quality, not just discriminative benchmarks。但 base model 绝对分数低 (~4/10) 限制了 这个 evidence 的说服力。审稿人可能 discount base model MT-Bench。 如果 GPU budget 不足应优先 drop 此实验。核心 claims 不依赖此结果。\\n\\n\\nbase model (非 instruct-tuned) 在 MT-Bench 上绝对分数有限 (~4/10)，因为 base model 缺乏 instruction-following alignment。但 relative ordering 仍有诊断价值: (1) KL30 retention ~92% (3.82/4.15) 高于短序列 downstream 的 retention (~85-90% on most tasks)，因为 MT-Bench 的 multi-turn format 更依赖 language modeling fluency (KL 直接优化的 objective) 而非 precise factual recall。 (2) Math/reasoning categories 退化最大 (~0.5 points) 因为这些 task 需要 precise step-by-step computation，每步的 sparse mask error 会 compound。 (3) Writing/humanities 几乎不受影响因为这些 task 依赖 dominant language patterns (high-activation neurons, natural sparsity floor 内保留的 neurons)。 (4) TEAL30 在 math/reasoning 上更差因为 magnitude mask 无法 preserve output distribution 的 tail (长尾 token predictions)，而 math 答案通常在 vocabulary distribution 的 tail 中。 base model 限制使 MT-Bench 的绝对值意义有限，但 \\\"KL 在 multi-turn generation 下 near-dense quality\\\" 的 relative finding 仍有叙事价值。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RULER Synthetic Long-Context Diagnostics\",\n    \"description\": \"RULER synthetic evaluation at 4K and 16K context, 3 task types: NIAH (needle-in-a-haystack), multi-key retrieval, variable tracking。 Fine-grained diagnostic complementing LongBench。P2 priority, deps on plan_010。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_4k_niah\": 92.5,\n      \"dense_4k_multikey\": 78.3,\n      \"dense_4k_vartrack\": 75.8,\n      \"dense_4k_avg\": 82.2,\n      \"kl30_4k_niah\": 88.2,\n      \"kl30_4k_multikey\": 71.5,\n      \"kl30_4k_vartrack\": 68.4,\n      \"kl30_4k_avg\": 76.0,\n      \"teal30_4k_niah\": 80.5,\n      \"teal30_4k_multikey\": 58.2,\n      \"teal30_4k_vartrack\": 55.8,\n      \"teal30_4k_avg\": 64.8,\n      \"dense_16k_niah\": 85.1,\n      \"dense_16k_multikey\": 62.4,\n      \"dense_16k_vartrack\": 58.2,\n      \"dense_16k_avg\": 68.6,\n      \"kl30_16k_niah\": 78.5,\n      \"kl30_16k_multikey\": 53.8,\n      \"kl30_16k_vartrack\": 49.2,\n      \"kl30_16k_avg\": 60.5,\n      \"teal30_16k_niah\": 68.2,\n      \"teal30_16k_multikey\": 40.5,\n      \"teal30_16k_vartrack\": 38.6,\n      \"teal30_16k_avg\": 49.1,\n      \"kl30_4k_to_16k_drop\": 15.5,\n      \"dense_4k_to_16k_drop\": 13.6,\n      \"teal30_4k_to_16k_drop\": 15.7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 8 (RULER): 3 conditions × 3 tasks × 2 lengths\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RULER 提供 fine-grained diagnostic: KL 的 advantage 在 multi-key 和 variable tracking 上最显著 (13-15pp over TEAL at 4K)，在 NIAH 上最小 (~8pp)。这与 \\\"KL captures joint neuron interaction\\\" 叙事一致——需要 multi-pattern activation 的 task 受益最大。 16K 数据表明 sparsity-induced degradation 不随 context length 加速， strengthening generalization claim。作为 P2，non-essential for core claims。\\n\\nRULER synthetic tasks 不需要 instruction following (与 MT-Bench 不同)，因此 base model 可以提供有意义的绝对分数。 (1) NIAH 对 sparsity 最 robust (KL30 retention 95% at 4K) 因为 needle retrieval 主要依赖 attention 定位 (未被 sparse)，FFN 只需 extract 和 copy 信息。 (2) Multi-key retrieval 和 variable tracking 对 sparsity 更敏感 (retention ~85-90%) 因为需要 FFN 同时处理多个 scattered information，neuron interaction quality 直接影响 cross-position information aggregation。 (3) 4K→16K degradation pattern: KL30 的 degradation rate (15.5pp) 接近 dense (13.6pp)， 而 TEAL30 (15.7pp) 与 KL30 相近。这说明 degradation 主要来自 Llama 3.1 8B 的 intrinsic long-context 能力限制，而非 sparsity 引入的额外退化。 (4) KL 在 multi-key task 上的优势最大 (KL 71.5 vs TEAL 58.2 at 4K)，因为 multi-key 需要 FFN 同时 activate 多个 retrieval patterns，KL 的 joint-interaction-aware masks 比 magnitude masks 更好地保留了这种 multi-pattern capacity。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":207,"startLine":1,"totalLines":207}}}
